---
import { issuesUrl } from '../data/release';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<section class="section faq" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="wrap faq__grid">
    <header class="section-head faq__head" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
      <h2 class="h2" id="faq-title">Good to know.</h2>
      <p class="muted">More in the <a href={`${base}docs/`}>CutOut guide</a>.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="faq__list">
      <details>
        <summary>Is CutOut really free?</summary>
        <p>Yes. There is no price, trial, subscription, in-app purchase, account or advertising.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Which Macs does it run on?</summary>
        <p>
          Macs with Apple silicon (M1 or later) running macOS 14 Sonoma or later. There is no Intel build yet. Best Quality removal took about 2.5
          seconds per image on an M1 in our tests.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Why does macOS warn me the first time I open it?</summary>
        <p>
          CutOut 0.1 is signed ad hoc rather than with an Apple Developer ID, and it isn’t notarized by Apple. macOS therefore asks you to confirm
          the first launch in System Settings ▸ Privacy &amp; Security. Before you do, check that the download’s SHA-256 matches the one on its
          release page. <a href={`${base}docs/#install`}>Step-by-step instructions</a>.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does CutOut upload my images?</summary>
        <p>
          No. Everything happens on your Mac. The app makes no network requests at all unless you start a model download yourself, and the full
          download already contains the model.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How well does it handle hair, fur — and glass?</summary>
        <p>
          Fur and hair work well; try the comparison above and zoom into the edge. Truly transparent things such as glass are harder: the model
          decides what is subject and what isn’t, so it can’t make a glass half-transparent. Use Refine Edges, the Magic Eraser or the Restore
          brush to finish those by hand.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What can I paste the result into?</summary>
        <p>
          Anything that accepts images from the clipboard. Copy puts a PNG with transparency on the clipboard, plus a TIFF that keeps the alpha
          channel for apps that prefer TIFF. Copy as JPEG is there too, with a warning, because JPEG can’t keep transparency.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Which files can it open and save?</summary>
        <p>
          It opens PNG, JPEG, HEIC, TIFF, GIF, BMP and WebP, by file, drag and drop or paste. It exports PNG and JPEG and saves <code>.cutout</code>
          projects that keep layers, masks and text editable. Images larger than 16,384 pixels on a side or 120 megapixels are scaled down on import,
          and CutOut tells you when it does.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is there a Windows version?</summary>
        <p>
          Not yet. CutOut’s image engine is written in portable Rust so that a native Windows app can reuse it, but that app hasn’t been built. This
          page will offer it only when a real, tested build exists.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How do I report a bug or ask for a feature?</summary>
        <p>
          Open an issue on <a href={issuesUrl} rel="noopener">GitHub</a> with your macOS version, Mac model and the steps that lead to the problem.
          Please don’t attach private photos; a screenshot of the window is usually enough.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 4fr) minmax(0, 8fr);
    gap: clamp(var(--s-6), 5vw, var(--s-9));
    align-items: start;
  }

  .faq__head {
    position: sticky;
    top: calc(var(--nav-h) + var(--s-7));
  }

  .faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
  }

  details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  summary {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    list-style: none;
    padding: var(--s-5) var(--s-8) var(--s-5) 0;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    line-height: 1.3;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  summary::after,
  summary::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    right: 6px;
    top: 50%;
    width: 16px;
    height: 1.75px;
    background: var(--ink);
    border-radius: 2px;
    transition: transform var(--t-med) var(--ease-out);
  }

  summary::before {
    transform: rotate(90deg);
  }

  details[open] summary::before {
    transform: rotate(0deg);
  }

  details p {
    padding-bottom: var(--s-6);
    max-width: 64ch;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  @media (max-width: 819px) {
    .faq__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .faq__head {
      position: static;
    }

    summary {
      font-size: 1.125rem;
    }
  }
</style>
